tmux-agent-herd

The agent-detection patterns in patterns/*.sh are derived from the agent-detection
manifests distributed with Herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr), located at
src/detect/manifests/*.toml in that project, which is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

This project reimplements the matching logic for tmux in shell and does not
incorporate Herdr's source code. The manifest string/regex patterns (e.g. the
Claude Code and Codex OSC-title spinner globs, the "do you want to proceed?" /
"requires approval" approval-form signatures) originate from those manifests.

